
### submit opens a pull request per branch, bottom first, and stacks them
$ git stack submit
submitting stack rooted at feat-a
pushed feat-a to origin (new branch)
pushed feat-b to origin (new branch)
opened #1 for feat-a onto main
opened #2 for feat-b onto feat-a
created GitHub stack #3: #1, #2
done.
[exit 0]
PR #1 feat-a -> main (open) a1
PR #2 feat-b -> feat-a (open) feat-b
    | - b1
    | - b2
stack #3: #1 #2

### a second submit finds the pull requests and the stack
GET repos/{owner}/{repo}
GET repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls head=octo:feat-a state=open
GET repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls head=octo:feat-b state=open
GET repos/{owner}/{repo}
GET repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls head=octo:feat-a state=open
POST repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls head=feat-a base=main title=a1 body=
GET repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls head=octo:feat-b state=open
POST repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls head=feat-b base=feat-a title=feat-b body=- b1
- b2
GET repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls/1
POST repos/{owner}/{repo}/stacks pull_requests[]=1 pull_requests[]=2
$ git stack submit
submitting stack rooted at feat-a
pushed feat-a to origin
pushed feat-b to origin
done.
[exit 0]
GET repos/{owner}/{repo}
GET repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls head=octo:feat-a state=open
GET repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls head=octo:feat-b state=open
GET repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls/1
GET repos/{owner}/{repo}/stacks/3
PR #1 feat-a -> main (open) a1
PR #2 feat-b -> feat-a (open) feat-b
    | - b1
    | - b2
stack #3: #1 #2

### submit extends the stack with a new branch on top
$ git stack submit
submitting stack rooted at feat-a
feat-a is up to date on origin
feat-b is up to date on origin
pushed feat-c to origin (new branch)
opened #4 for feat-c onto feat-b
added #4 to GitHub stack #3
done.
[exit 0]
PR #1 feat-a -> main (open) a1
PR #2 feat-b -> feat-a (open) feat-b
    | - b1
    | - b2
PR #4 feat-c -> feat-b (open) c1
stack #3: #1 #2 #4

### submit retargets a pull request whose base is not its parent
$ git stack submit
submitting stack rooted at feat-a
pushed feat-a to origin (new branch)
pushed feat-b to origin (new branch)
opened #2 for feat-a onto main
retargeted #1 (feat-b) onto feat-a
created GitHub stack #3: #2, #1
done.
[exit 0]
PR #1 feat-b -> feat-a (open) feat-b
PR #2 feat-a -> main (open) a1
stack #3: #2 #1

### submit leaves a GitHub stack that does not match, and says so
$ git stack submit
submitting stack rooted at feat-a
pushed feat-a to origin (new branch)
pushed feat-b to origin (new branch)
warning: GitHub stack #4 holds #1, #3, but this stack is #1, #2; leaving it as it is -- fix it on github.com, or run 'git stack mode local'
done.
[exit 0]
PR #1 feat-a -> main (open) feat-a
PR #2 feat-b -> feat-a (open) feat-b
PR #3 feat-x -> feat-a (open) feat-x
stack #4: #1 #3

### a branch with no commits cannot become a pull request
$ git stack submit
error: 'feat-a' has no commits of its own; GitHub cannot open a pull request for it
[exit 1]
feat-a on origin: none

### a failing gh call stops submit with gh's message
$ git stack submit
submitting stack rooted at feat-a
pushed feat-a to origin (new branch)
pushed feat-b to origin (new branch)
opened #1 for feat-a onto main
opened #2 for feat-b onto feat-a
error: gh api failed: gh: injected failure for 'POST repos/{owner}/{repo}/stacks pull_requests[]=1 pull_requests[]=2' (HTTP 422)
[exit 1]
PR #1 feat-a -> main (open) a1
PR #2 feat-b -> feat-a (open) feat-b
    | - b1
    | - b2

### local mode submit never calls gh
$ git stack submit
submitting stack rooted at feat-a
pushed feat-a to origin (new branch)
done.
[exit 0]


### mode github stacks the pull requests that already exist
$ git stack mode github
stack rooted at feat-a is now github
set stack.trunkUpstream to true, so github stacks follow the trunk GitHub merges into (this applies to every stack in the repository)
created GitHub stack #3: #1, #2
1 branch(es) have no pull request yet; 'git stack submit' opens them
[exit 0]
PR #1 feat-a -> main (open) feat-a
PR #2 feat-b -> feat-a (open) feat-b
stack #3: #1 #2
